# libambx

`libambx` is the Ruby USB driver for Philips amBX lights and compatible
devices. It was originally created as **Combustd** by Martijn de Boer and
Gert-Jan de Boer; its original BSD 3-Clause licence and attribution are
preserved in this repository.

This gem provides low-level access to each physically connected amBX USB set.
Home Assistant support will live in the separate `ambx2mqtt` project; it is
not published or runnable from this repository yet.

## Using one physical USB set

Discovering devices does not open them. Each returned device has a stable
identity for configuration and owns only its own USB handle.

```ruby
require "libambx"

Ambx.devices.each do |device|
  device.open
  device.write([ 0x01, Lights::LEFT, ProtocolDefinitions::SET_LIGHT_COLOR, 255, 0, 0 ])
ensure
  device&.close
end
```

`device.identity` prefers the USB serial number and falls back to its USB port
path. `Device#write` returns `false` when that device disappears; other open
devices remain available. This driver reports requested writes only and does
not read actual light state back from the hardware.

## Legacy broadcast compatibility

Existing applications can keep using `Ambx.connect`, `Ambx.open`, and
`Ambx.close`. Use `Ambx.write_all(bytes)` to explicitly broadcast a command to
every set opened through that legacy facade.

`Ambx.write(bytes)` remains as a deprecated alias for one compatibility
release and prints a migration warning once per process. A legacy broadcast
stops and closes its legacy device collection if one set disconnects.

## Development

See [INSTALL](INSTALL). The project keeps the original Combustd examples and
applications where they remain supported.
